  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466500",
      "title": "Understanding Shared Modules",
      "lectureOrder": 653,
      "videoOrder": 601,
      "sourceHash": "6cc183c222a4f535226e6bb87e359dd2e63f982c889ad87929128ce1fa0362f4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "Instructor: We had a look at feature modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "now let's dive into shared modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "Now, what's a shared module?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "In this hypothetical app here, we got two feature modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "and of course, we would also have an app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "but it's not important for the shared module here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 21.6,
          "en": "So, we got two feature modules, products and sales.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.6,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "And as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "these two modules only differ in one component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "The products module has the products component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 29.97,
          "en": "here on the left,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.97,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "and the sales module, on the bottom right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "has a sales component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "All the other components and directives they use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "are essentially the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "Now, you can put such shared features, shared components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "directives, and other modules even, into a shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "which you then import into both other modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "This again, is a great step to avoid code duplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "and have leaner modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 59.97,
          "en": "Now, let's see this in practice in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 61.38,
          "en": "In our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 66.38,
          "en": "we have no real shared features across our feature modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "If we have a look at the shopping list module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 72.89,
          "en": "and the recipes module, the only thing they have in common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.89,
          "end": 76.02,
          "en": "is the NT common module, which unlocks NGF.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.02,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "Now, we could put this into a separate, shared module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "and we will actually, but this alone would not be worth it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.99,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "because then we just import our shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.64,
          "en": "which exports the common module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.64,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "instead of just importing the common module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.86,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "So, we wouldn't win much by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "But in theory, in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "we have more shared content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "We have the alert, the loading spinner, and the placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "and the dropdown directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 100.5,
          "en": "The data storage service not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.5,
          "end": 103.173,
          "en": "because services are special, as you will learn soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "So therefore, here in the shared folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 109.95,
          "en": "I'll create a shared dot module dot Typescript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.95,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "And you can have multiple shared modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 113.82,
          "en": "and, therefore, they don't have to be named",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.82,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "shared dot module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 116.97,
          "en": "If you only have one, it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "Otherwise, you should give them a name that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "kind of, summarizes which features you're grouping in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "Now here, I'll name it just shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "and export a class shared module, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 130.95,
          "en": "and just as before, this is a regular angular module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "and it, therefore, will receive the at NG module decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.51,
          "en": "Now, the idea here is that you still now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.51,
          "end": 142.56,
          "en": "declare and import anything into this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 142.56,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "that might be used by other modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "but since every module works standalone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 151.32,
          "en": "to then also make these things available in other modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.32,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "you will also export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "all these things which you're importing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "So therefore, here, for example we add a declaration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.87,
          "en": "to declare our alert component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.87,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "to declare our loading spinner component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "and make sure you add all the NT import props at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 172.47,
          "en": "to declare our placeholder directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "and our dropdown directive, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.44299999999998,
          "en": "And again, make sure to add all these imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "And this would be it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 185.58,
          "en": "And let's now also say, we also wanna share some services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.58,
          "end": 188.52,
          "en": "like the common module, not services, excuse me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.52,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "I mean modules, like the common module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 192.72,
          "en": "which we import from at angular common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.72,
          "end": 194.73,
          "en": "So, I add this import here too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 198,
          "en": "And then, since we don't wanna use these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 198,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "in the shared module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "but import the shared module into other modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 205.17000000000002,
          "en": "we can export this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.17000000000002,
          "end": 208.53,
          "en": "And we export the alert component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 208.53,
          "end": 212.673,
          "en": "the loading spinner component, the placeholder directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.66899999999998,
          "end": 217.23,
          "en": "the dropdown directive, and also the common module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 217.23,
          "end": 219.99,
          "en": "And now, the idea is that wherever we import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.99,
          "end": 222.24,
          "en": "the shared module, we have access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.24,
          "end": 225.3,
          "en": "to all these features which we initialize here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.3,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "So, in other modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.32,
          "en": "where we want to use one or all of these features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.32,
          "end": 231.54,
          "en": "we don't have to add them to their modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "we just import the shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 236.34,
          "en": "and we got access because we're exporting all these stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 236.34,
          "end": 238.89,
          "en": "If we wouldn't export it, we would not have access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 242.58,
          "en": "So, let's now use the shared module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 246.72,
          "en": "Let's go to our shopping list module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 246.72,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "and there we can at least now replace the common module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "although that alone would not be worth it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 254.64,
          "en": "but to demonstrate it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 254.64,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "and we replaced it with the shared module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 257.7,
          "end": 259.86,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned it, that's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 261.03,
          "en": "It's not worth it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 261.03,
          "end": 264.78,
          "en": "because the only thing we really need from the shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 267.81,
          "en": "in the shopping list module is the common module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 267.81,
          "end": 271.35,
          "en": "and therefore we replaced one module import with another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 271.35,
          "end": 273.51,
          "en": "But if we would use the alert component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 273.51,
          "end": 276.48,
          "en": "or the placeholder directive, or the dropdown directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 276.48,
          "end": 278.79,
          "en": "then we would gain much more from that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 278.79,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "because now we don't have to add all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "to declarations here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 283.86,
          "en": "We just bring in the shared module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 285.51,
          "en": "and we got access to all the things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 285.51,
          "end": 289.14,
          "en": "declared in the shared module and exported there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 292.23,
          "en": "So in the recipes component, in recipes module, excuse me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 292.23,
          "end": 293.67,
          "en": "we can do the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 295.35,
          "en": "We got the common module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 295.35,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "Now, we can remove that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 301.95,
          "en": "and instead simply bring in that shared module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 305.43,
          "en": "Again, here not super useful, but to practice this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 305.43,
          "end": 308.46,
          "en": "Of course, we can now remove the common module import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 308.46,
          "end": 310.83,
          "en": "and just import the shared module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 310.83,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "Now with that, if we try to save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 314.07,
          "en": "we'll face an issue, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 314.07,
          "end": 316.44,
          "en": "As the app reloads we get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 316.44,
          "end": 318.36,
          "en": "that the dropdown directive is part of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 318.36,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "the declaration of two modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 323.52,
          "en": "and that is now another super important concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 323.52,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "you gotta understand about modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 330.9,
          "en": "You can only define, or declare, components, directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 330.9,
          "end": 332.43,
          "en": "and pipes once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 332.43,
          "end": 334.38,
          "en": "You can't do that multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 334.38,
          "end": 338.1,
          "en": "You can import a module into multiple imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 338.1,
          "end": 340.83,
          "en": "So, it is fine if we import the router module here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 340.83,
          "end": 344.1,
          "en": "in the recipes module and also in the shopping list module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 344.1,
          "end": 349.1,
          "en": "Imports are okay, but declarations are not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 349.23,
          "end": 351.54,
          "en": "If you declare the shopping list component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 351.54,
          "end": 353.31,
          "en": "in the shopping list module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 353.31,
          "end": 357,
          "en": "you must not declare it anywhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 357,
          "end": 358.8,
          "en": "Even if you need it in another module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 360.45,
          "en": "you must not declare it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 360.45,
          "end": 363.12,
          "en": "The solution then, instead, is to export it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
